An intake spans two systems: applicants use the **admissions portal**, staff work in the **staff
dashboard**. This is the staff side end to end.

## 1. Publish the prospectus

**Students → Prospectus** (also reachable from **Administration**). This is what applicants read
before applying, so it goes up before you announce the intake.

Applicants' view: [Reading the Prospectus](/docs/admissions-prospectus).

## 2. Applications come in

Applicants sign in with a one-time code, complete the form and submit. Once submitted, an
application is **locked** to them — they cannot keep editing it. See
[Applying to a School](/docs/admissions-applying).

## 3. Pull them into the dashboard

Open **Students → Admissions** and select **Fetch from Portal**. It reports how many were **synced**
and how many **skipped** — skipped generally meaning already imported.

Sync regularly through an open intake rather than once at the end; the dashboard only knows about
applications that have been fetched.

## 4. Review and score

The admissions list can be filtered and sorted by name, address, religion, **total score** and
**status**. Open any row for the full application and its uploaded documents.

**Total score** is what you rank on. Whatever your criteria are, they end up as this number, so make
sure it is being filled in consistently before you start comparing applicants.

Export the list — admission ID, name, address, religion and total score — for offline review or a
selection meeting.

## 5. Take the application fee

Two routes, and they end in the same place:

- **Online** — the applicant pays by card in the portal. A *pending* status is not a failure; it
  resolves. See [Paying Your Application Fee](/docs/admissions-payment).
- **At the office** — cash, cheque or transfer, recorded at **Students → Fee Counter** (the same
  screen appears as **Admission Fees** under Accounting). See
  [Paying at the School Office](/docs/admissions-paying-at-the-office).

Admission fees land in the same ledger as everything else, so they flow into
[day close](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-day-close) and
[reconciliation](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-reconciliation) normally.

## 6. Convert to students

Accepted applicants become students. Have the classes ready first — see
[Add a Class](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-add-a-class) — because a student needs one at enrolment, and
the class cannot be changed afterwards by editing the record.

## 7. After the intake

- Check [fee schedules](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-fee-setup) cover the new classes.
- Issue [ID cards](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-id-cards) — no RFID means no attendance.
- Parents register themselves against their child's Student ID —
  [Registering as a Parent](/docs/shared-parent-registration).

## For a school group

Head office sees the whole group's intake at **Reports → Admissions**, but cannot open an individual
branch's screens. See [Head Office & Group Reporting](/docs/shared-head-office-group-reporting).
